# Your live config -- config.default.yaml is the tracked template; see
# its header comment. Bootstrapped automatically on first run, never
# touched by git again after that, so dashboard/hand edits survive every
# `git pull` instead of risking being discarded as "local changes that
# would be overwritten by merge."
config.yaml
config.yaml.bak
config.yaml.tmp
# Each profile's own strategy/risk definition -- tracked, unlike
# config.yaml above: these are treated as versioned strategy logic (so a
# new machine/Pi gets new strategies via `git pull` instead of a manual
# copy), not per-machine account config. The tradeoff: an Edit Settings
# change on one machine can now show as a tracked diff or conflict with a
# `git pull` bringing in a change to the same profile, the same as any
# other tracked file -- config.yaml itself stays gitignored specifically
# to avoid that.
profiles/*.bak
profiles/*.tmp
.env
